# No `# expect:`: src/tychoc.c:7602 says `element 2 of a bounded[4]int literal
# is the wrong type`, tychoc1 says `array elements must all have the same type`.
# The two name different subjects and neither is a substring of the other, so an
# expectation could only assert one of them -- and `make test` scores it against
# ./tychoc1 (tests/run.sh:102). Recorded, not ported.
fn main():
    b: bounded[4]int = [1, "a"]
    println(str(len(b)))
